.TH "BUNDLE\-PLUGIN" "1" "May 2026" ""
.SH "NAME"
\fBbundle\-plugin\fR \- Manage Bundler plugins
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
\fBbundle plugin\fR install PLUGINS [\-\-source=SOURCE] [\-\-version=VERSION] [\-\-git=GIT] [\-\-branch=BRANCH|\-\-ref=REF] [\-\-path=PATH]
.br
\fBbundle plugin\fR uninstall PLUGINS [\-\-all]
.br
\fBbundle plugin\fR list
.br
\fBbundle plugin\fR help [COMMAND]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
You can install, uninstall, and list plugin(s) with this command to extend functionalities of Bundler\.
.SH "SUB\-COMMANDS"
.SS "install"
Install the given plugin(s)\.
.P
For example, \fBbundle plugin install bundler\-graph\fR will install bundler\-graph gem from globally configured sources (defaults to RubyGems\.org)\. Note that the global source specified in Gemfile is ignored\.
.P
\fBOPTIONS\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-source=SOURCE\fR
Install the plugin gem from a specific source, rather than from globally configured sources\.
.IP
Example: \fBbundle plugin install bundler\-graph \-\-source https://example\.com\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-version=VERSION\fR
Specify a version of the plugin gem to install via \fB\-\-version\fR\.
.IP
Example: \fBbundle plugin install bundler\-graph \-\-version 0\.2\.1\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-git=GIT\fR
Install the plugin gem from a Git repository\. You can use standard Git URLs like:
.IP
\fBssh://[user@]host\.xz[:port]/path/to/repo\.git\fR
.br
\fBhttp[s]://host\.xz[:port]/path/to/repo\.git\fR
.br
\fB/path/to/repo\fR
.br
\fBfile:///path/to/repo\fR
.IP
Example: \fBbundle plugin install bundler\-graph \-\-git https://github\.com/rubygems/bundler\-graph\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-branch=BRANCH\fR
When you specify \fB\-\-git\fR, you can use \fB\-\-branch\fR to use\.
.TP
\fB\-\-ref=REF\fR
When you specify \fB\-\-git\fR, you can use \fB\-\-ref\fR to specify any tag, or commit hash (revision) to use\.
.TP
\fB\-\-path=PATH\fR
Install the plugin gem from a local path\.
.IP
Example: \fBbundle plugin install bundler\-graph \-\-path \.\./bundler\-graph\fR
.SS "uninstall"
Uninstall the plugin(s) specified in PLUGINS\.
.P
\fBOPTIONS\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-all\fR
Uninstall all the installed plugins\. If no plugin is installed, then it does nothing\.
.SS "list"
List the installed plugins and available commands\.
.P
No options\.
.SS "help"
Describe subcommands or one specific subcommand\.
.P
No options\.
.SH "HOOKS"
A plugin can run code at defined points of Bundler's work by registering a hook\. In the plugin's \fBplugins\.rb\fR, pass one of the event constants of \fBBundler::Plugin::Events\fR and a block to \fBBundler::Plugin::API\.hook\fR\. Bundler loads a plugin that registers a hook for an event when that event fires, and calls the block with the arguments listed for the event below\.
.IP "" 4
.nf
Bundler::Plugin::API\.hook Bundler::Plugin::Events::GEM_BEFORE_INSTALL_ALL do |dependencies|
  puts "about to install #{dependencies\.map(&:name)\.join(", ")}"
end
.fi
.IP "" 0
.P
The events fire in the order listed here\.
.P
\fBGEMFILE EVALUATION\fR
.TP
\fBGEM_BEFORE_EVAL\fR (\fBbefore\-eval\fR)
Called before the Gemfile is evaluated, with the path to the Gemfile and the path to the lockfile (\fBnil\fR when there is no lockfile)\.
.TP
\fBGEM_AFTER_EVAL\fR (\fBafter\-eval\fR)
Called after the Gemfile is evaluated, with the resulting \fBBundler::Definition\fR\.
.P
\fBINSTALLATION\fR
.TP
\fBGEM_BEFORE_INSTALL_ALL\fR (\fBbefore\-install\-all\fR)
Called before any gem is installed, with an Array of the \fBBundler::Dependency\fR objects declared in the Gemfile\.
.TP
\fBGEM_BEFORE_FETCH\fR (\fBbefore\-fetch\fR)
Called before each individual gem is downloaded from a remote source, with a spec\-like object responding to the \fBGem::Specification\fR API (for example a \fBBundler::EndpointSpecification\fR or \fBBundler::RemoteSpecification\fR)\. Does not fire for a gem that is already present in the download cache\.
.TP
\fBGEM_AFTER_FETCH\fR (\fBafter\-fetch\fR)
Called after each individual gem is downloaded from a remote source, with the same spec\-like object as \fBGEM_BEFORE_FETCH\fR\. Also fires when the download fails\.
.TP
\fBGIT_BEFORE_FETCH\fR (\fBbefore\-git\-fetch\fR)
Called before a git source is fetched or checked out, with the \fBBundler::Source::Git\fR being fetched\.
.TP
\fBGIT_AFTER_FETCH\fR (\fBafter\-git\-fetch\fR)
Called after a git source is fetched or checked out, with the same \fBBundler::Source::Git\fR\. Also fires when the fetch or checkout fails\.
.TP
\fBGEM_BEFORE_INSTALL\fR (\fBbefore\-install\fR)
Called before each individual gem is installed, with a \fBBundler::ParallelInstaller::SpecInstallation\fR\. Its \fBstate\fR, \fBerror\fR and \fBpost_install_message\fR are not set yet, as nothing has been installed\.
.TP
\fBGEM_AFTER_INSTALL\fR (\fBafter\-install\fR)
Called after each individual gem is installed, with the same \fBBundler::ParallelInstaller::SpecInstallation\fR\. If its \fBstate\fR is \fBfailed\fR, \fBerror\fR holds the exception; if the \fBstate\fR is \fBsuccess\fR, a \fBpost_install_message\fR may be present\.
.TP
\fBGEM_AFTER_INSTALL_ALL\fR (\fBafter\-install\-all\fR)
Called after all gems are installed, with an Array of the \fBBundler::Dependency\fR objects declared in the Gemfile\.
.P
\fBREQUIRE\fR
.P
These events fire from \fBBundler\.require\fR\.
.TP
\fBGEM_BEFORE_REQUIRE_ALL\fR (\fBbefore\-require\-all\fR)
Called before any gem is required, with an Array of the \fBBundler::Dependency\fR objects being required\.
.TP
\fBGEM_BEFORE_REQUIRE\fR (\fBbefore\-require\fR)
Called before each individual gem is required, with its \fBBundler::Dependency\fR\.
.TP
\fBGEM_AFTER_REQUIRE\fR (\fBafter\-require\fR)
Called after each individual gem is required, with its \fBBundler::Dependency\fR\.
.TP
\fBGEM_AFTER_REQUIRE_ALL\fR (\fBafter\-require\-all\fR)
Called after all gems are required, with an Array of the \fBBundler::Dependency\fR objects that were required\.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.IP "\(bu" 4
How to write a Bundler plugin \fIhttps://guides\.rubygems\.org/bundler_plugins/\fR
